14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Wyoming law sets out when a person occupying land can claim title by adverse possession, and how an owner can remove someone who has no right to be there.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>An action for recovery of title or possession of land can only be brought within 10 years after the cause of action accrues. (W.S. 1-3-103; <a href='https://wyoleg.gov/statutes/compress/title01.pdf?section=1-3-103' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Forcible entry and detainer (circuit court) lies where the defendant is a settler or occupier of land without color of title to which the complainant has the right of possession. (W.S. 1-21-1002(a)(v); <a href='https://wyoleg.gov/NXT/gateway.dll/2026%20Wyoming%20Statutes/2026%20Titles/1/53/63?f=templates&fn=document-frameset.htm' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Notice to quit must be served at least 3 days before commencing a forcible entry or detainer action. (W.S. 1-21-1003; <a href='https://wyoleg.gov/NXT/gateway.dll/2026%20Wyoming%20Statutes/2026%20Titles/1/53/63?f=templates&fn=document-frameset.htm' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A pending forcible entry or detainer action does not bar an action of ejectment. (W.S. 1-21-1016; <a href='https://wyoleg.gov/NXT/gateway.dll/2026%20Wyoming%20Statutes/2026%20Titles/1/53/63?f=templates&fn=document-frameset.htm' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Criminal trespass: entering or remaining on another&#x27;s land or premises knowing one is not authorized, or after notice to depart (personal communication or posted signs); misdemeanor, up to 6 months jail, fine up to $750, or both. (W.S. 6-3-303; <a href='https://wyoleg.gov/statutes/compress/title06.pdf?section=6-3-303' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Violently taking or keeping possession of land without authority of law is a misdemeanor (fine up to $750). (W.S. 6-3-306; <a href='https://wyoleg.gov/statutes/compress/title06.pdf?section=6-3-303' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Wyoming?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Wyoming houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><h2>Wyoming Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession FAQ</h2><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Can a squatter take ownership of my Wyoming house?</h3><p> Check the statute and talk to a Wyoming attorney about your facts.</p><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/wyoming-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Wyoming guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-wyoming/'>We buy houses in Wyoming</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://wyoleg.gov/statutes/compress/title01.pdf?section=1-3-103' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>W.S. 1-3-103</a></li><li><a href='https://wyoleg.gov/NXT/gateway.dll/2026%20Wyoming%20Statutes/2026%20Titles/1/53/63?f=templates&fn=document-frameset.htm' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>W.S. 1-21-1002(a)(v)</a></li><li><a href='https://wyoleg.gov/statutes/compress/title06.pdf?section=6-3-303' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>W.S. 6-3-303</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Wyoming Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can a squatter take ownership of my Wyoming house?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Only by meeting every requirement of the adverse possession statute cited above for the full period. Check the statute and talk to a Wyoming attorney about your facts.\"}}]}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Wyoming\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-wyoming/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Wyoming Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/wyoming-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Wyoming Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession", "rank_math_description": "Wyoming squatters rights and adverse possession: what the statutes say and how owners remove occupants or sell. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "wyoming squatters rights"}]